  "summary": "The complete 11→12→13 path is continuous for a mathematically prepared beginner with the explicitly named earlier tensor, masking, training and evaluation concepts. Chapter 10 ends by separating retrieval from generation; chapter 11 turns that limitation into tests of semantic alignment, image-dependent correctness and retained text ability. Chapter 12 reuses the same feature-insertion interface while introducing waveform-to-log-mel concepts before they are required, then separates tone tasks, held-out-speaker digit recognition and an ASR-to-chat route. Chapter 13 deliberately restarts from text SFT and evaluation rather than requiring image/audio mastery; it builds full-answer scoring and fixed-reference DPO, then explains finite-card PPO with separately identified scorer, critic, old policy and reference. The chapter 14 boundary returns to controlled architecture changes. Actual promised chapter 20 targets preserve the larger pretrained base, optional LoRA, separate ASR and natural-media evaluation limits. Complete assigned reading, listed prerequisites, 30 personal SVG views and meaningful browser clicks support a pass; no blocking continuity issue remains.",
